<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <head>
        <title>A shrink-to-fit flex label keeps its text on one line</title>
        <!-- Engine bug pinned: the intrinsic max-content scan and the line
             breaker folded f32 widths differently (per-word subtotals plus a
             subtract-based fit test), so a box sized to its own measured
             max-content wrapped its last word ("Format Painter" became
             "Format / Painter"). The marker band below the labels turns the
             wrap into a large geometric shift. -->
        <style type="text/css">
            * { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
            body { width: 800px; background: #ffffff; font-family: sans-serif; }
            .row { display: flex; flex-direction: row; }
            .btn { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;
                   background: #dde8f5; padding: 2px 6px; margin: 4px;
                   font-size: 16px; color: #222222; }
            .marker { height: 120px; background: #2a579a; }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="btn">Format Painter</div>
            <div class="btn">Decrease Indent</div>
            <div class="btn">No Spacing</div>
        </div>
        <div class="marker"></div>
    </body>
</html>
